https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-05-prefix-free-stepanov/</guid><description>Prefix-freeness is the property that lifts the free-monoid construction into bit space.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-05-prefix-free-stepanov/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Category Theory</media:title></media:content><category>C++</category><category>generic-programming</category><category>codecs</category><category>information-theory</category><category>category-theory</category><category>monoids</category></item><item><title>Free Algebras: Why Lists and Polynomials Are Universal</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-free-algebra-stepanov/</link><pubDate>Fri, 13 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-free-algebra-stepanov/</guid><description>The free monoid on a set is the type of lists over that set. The universal property says fold is the unique homomorphism from lists to any monoid. This explains why lists, multisets, and polynomials appear everywhere.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-03-free-algebra-stepanov/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Category Theory</media:title></media:content><category>C++</category><category>generic-programming</category><category>algorithms</category><category>monoids</category><category>category-theory</category></item><item><title>Duality: The Hidden Structure of Opposites</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-19-duality-stepanov/</link><pubDate>Mon, 19 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-01-19-duality-stepanov/</guid><description>Many structures come in pairs: forward/reverse AD, push/pull iteration, encode/decode. Recognizing duality lets you transfer theorems and insights between domains.</description><media:content url